Result

The TE₁₀ mode was successfully simulated for the WR-90 rectangular waveguide. The cutoff frequency was found to be approximately 6.56 GHz, and the propagation constant at 10 GHz was approximately 199 rad/m. Since 10 GHz is greater than the cutoff frequency, the TE₁₀ mode propagates successfully through the waveguide. The corresponding E-field and H-field distributions were obtained.
